// M4.2: a place is a base plus a chain of FIELD names. An ELEMENT (`xs[0]`) is not one — its index is a
// runtime value, so no static rule can decide whether two children's indices overlap. `placePath` reports
// that by returning the empty path, the same "not a statically-nameable place" signal the view model
// rejects a borrow host on, and `spawn` refuses it here rather than pretending to a disjointness proof it
// cannot make. (Rust is conservative about the index projection for the same reason — it is why
// `split_at_mut` has to exist.)
//
// Splitting one buffer across workers is `parallel_for`'s job: it slices a container into K
// non-overlapping sub-views, which IS the proof this rule cannot supply. Must fail to compile.
import { std::concurrent::Isolate, std::collections::DynamicArray };

type value Acc { public int32 total; public ctor make() { this.total = 0; return this; } }

fn void step(ref Acc a) { a.total = a.total + 1; }

fn int32 main() {
    DynamicArray<Acc> xs = DynamicArray.empty();
    xs.add(item: Acc.make());
    scope {
        spawn step(a: ref xs[0]);   // ERROR: an element names no static place
    }
    return 0;
}
